      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For a feature request I think you should be clear on exactly what's intended to happen. If I type something in german are you intending for it to be machine translated for you to the language you specify? \n\nI think VRChat passing text to a translation service would go against the goal of VRChat to treat the chat box as close to voice as possible.\n\nWith the OSC stuff you could make/find a program that sends text input through a service and outputs to your chat box.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-05T01:08:19.780Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Imagine a setting where you can pick any language you want. Similar as Google translate, but when people talk in Chatbox, it will automatically translate to however you set your language. This will be fantastic for people that can communicate to one another with different languages.",
